  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a direct relationship between 3Alpha-Hydroxyurs-12-Ene and HCC1937, mediated through Leukocyte antigen CD37. This pathway is supported by multiple high-scoring connections, all of which indicate that 3Alpha-Hydroxyurs-12-Ene acts as a target for Leukocyte antigen CD37, which in turn targets HCC1937. The distinct structural variations in the target molecules—such as different stereochemical configurations—do not alter the core mechanism of interaction, suggesting a general structural compatibility that allows 3Alpha-Hydroxyurs-12-Ene to bind to CD37 and subsequently affect HCC1937. The consistent presence of Leukocyte antigen CD37 as a target across all three paths reinforces the reliability of this relationship. The evidence does not provide direct evidence of how 3Alpha-Hydroxyurs-12-Ene interacts with HCC1937 at a molecular level, but the shared pathway through CD37 offers a plausible mechanism for the observed relationship.",
